A||||13||Shaun41178||Fiero vs 94 Trans Am 6 speed||||14||
Z||000000||Shaun41178||03-04-2000||06:05 PM||||Last night was a good night for me. I got into a race with a 3rd gen which was no competition, a Dadge truck like a early 90s model with loud exhaust for one mod, and also a newer Dodge Truck a Dakota with either the V8 Magnum or the V6 Magnum. I don't remember the emblem on the side of it exactly. I won all of those rather easily so I will tell you about this T/A<P>I turned at a red light and noticed a 4th Gen T/A that was going to be going my way once his light turned green so I kept it slow but his light was red too long so I pulled off and waited till he went by. I caught up and gave him a rev and a few jumps but nothing. He then pulled in behind me and put his blinker on for the upcoming light so I turned too. It was a white T/A 94 (later found out) with a 6 speed. He had a windshiled sticker that said Trans Am and a hatch cover protector thing to keep the sun rays out the back or something and some Tristar chrome rims. So anyways we get going and at about 40 or so we both punch it and we took it all the way up to 85-90 or so. The results? He only pulled a half car on me!!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  So we caught a light and he said to pull over and I said sure but asked him first if he wanted to go from the light. He said sure. I powerbrake it up, light turns green and I just nail it off the line nitrous and all and tires squeel for a moment and I am gone. He spun from what I could tell and at around 50 I had 2 cars or so on him so I shutdown and we pull off. He tells me that he has a LT-4 engine in his car with about 1k miles on it. He has a cam from what he said, new crank and pistons (I don't know what comes with an LT-4 engine) 1.6 rockers, headers, catback, a centerforce clutch. I was surprised I was able to hang with this guy. I figured he was pushing about 330 hp or so. Possibly more??? And to only pull a half a car I was ecstatic. I will say this though, he did shift fairly slow and when we talked he said he was still trying to feel it out and he thinks that the shift linkage might need to be adjusted. Well just thought I would share my story with you all. I plan to go back out and look for some more trouble tonight too and perhaps run into him again.<P>------------------<BR>The Car: <BR>85 Pontiac Fiero GT<BR>Drivetrain:<BR>2.8 V6 3.08 FD 3 spd auto <BR>MODS:<BR>Crane HI-6S ignition <BR>PS-91 Coil<BR>Accel 8.8 mm wires<BR>Throttle Body bypass<BR>K&N air filter<BR>Ported exhaust manifolds<BR>Underdrive Pulley<BR>NOS 70 hp shot<P>Best E.T. to Date: <BR>R/T:.707<BR>60': 1.895 on street tires, 215/60/r14 to be exact.<BR>330': 5.636<BR>1/8: 8.848 MPH: 75.60<BR>1000': 11.683<BR>1/4: 14.161 MPH: 89.18 <BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178</A> <P>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Ferrari355||03-04-2000||06:42 PM||||Sorry to sound rude or anything remember i love Fiero's, but how could a Fiero beat a 4th gen Trans Am? Seems weird. We have never raced a Fiero but i figured our 89 Trans Am 5.0 would be close or smoke a fiero. But i've never seen or been in a Fiero when it's been floored even though i have a few times in my '84 SE 4 banger, it was funny. Anyway, just wondering. TTYL, bye...<P>Alex....||||reg||5
Z||000002||Monkeyman||03-04-2000||08:14 PM||||My guess is that the nitrous oxide helped.||||reg||1
Z||000003||kidzwheelz||03-04-2000||09:28 PM||||  I also don't want to put down an obviously strong Fiero, but I'm definately thinking that not only did this guy not know how to drive his T/A, but I don't buy that he has all the hi-po parts he said he had. I know that a V-6 Fiero can hold it's own against some heavy competition, but I have a 1990 GTA with a few mods and an automatic, and you wouldn't be leaving me at the light. Sounds like you have a really nice car though!||||reg||11
Z||000004||AL||03-04-2000||11:43 PM||||i love fieros also but my 89gta would eat a fiero for lunch, but it sounds like you have a bad a$$ FIERO, PUT A PIC of it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||03-05-2000||12:32 AM||||I'm biased too cause my car has nitrous too. but. just play the numbers game here... we'll use my car cause i don't have shauns dyno sheet here... ok @ 1500rpm my car puts down 243.6lbft of torque and weighs in with me in the car and 1.2 tank of fuel at 2173lbs. 4th gen TA 320hp, 300lbft at 3800rpm and he weighs in at 3500lbs roughly. I'm on the gas in the nitrous and at the next light before he even knew what hit him! All our weight is over the drive wheels the TA.. uun NO. His car makes 300lbft at the flywheel! mine makes 310 at the flywheel and weighs less! LOTS less. Now if Shaun had run him in the 1/4 or 1/2 mile he would (on my own experiance) would have kepted up then bailed out cause a cop is near... or just BARELY lost at the 1/2 mile mark cause he lacks on the top end. (as do I) I have YET to lose a standing light to light! A rolling light well a couple Supra turbos got me there... I've sen shauns dyno #s and the rank righ up there with a TA, on the bottle. Many people love their Fiero but few ever actually push them to their limits, and thats the best part about it... said unsuspecting Moostang or TA aren't looking for it and when they get pulled by it or paced by one they gain respect that the fiero deserves. And that gives a tarnished reputation to that a big headed high HP guy that SOOO many people looked up to...  ".. watch out here comes a guy in that Fiero"... never thought I'd here that till last thursday night at the local monthly car show... Don't think i've ever been prouder of my car, that that moment a mustang owner surrenders voulntarily! VIVA LA Fiero! ||||reg||1
